  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 173.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp1n1ppp/4pn2/1Q3b2/2BP4/2N5/PP3PPP/R1B1K1NR w KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "Qb3",
    "Nbd7",
    "Qb5",
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "We hit the queenside with the queen to b3, forking two of Black's weak pawns to win one; Black defends with ...Nbd7, we slide to b5, and Black shores up with ...e6. Now the discipline is to finish development, not to lunge the knight into c7."
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 213.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp1n1ppp/4pn2/5b2/2BP4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1B1K2R w KQkq - 2 11",
   "line": [
    "Qb6",
    "Qxb6",
    "Nf3",
    "Qd8"
   ],
   "spoken": "A pawn up and pressing, the plan is patient: complete development, castle, and if Black keeps chasing the queen, calmly sidestep — to a6 or c6 — without ever allowing a draw by repetition. His rook sorties to the queenside would only misplace the rook, and a well-timed knight-takes-d7 with check could win it. Once the IQP has done its job we trade it off and turn the attack on the king.",
